---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Play online
description: Weekly Discord tournaments every Saturday and Sunday, monthly async leagues on webcam, Cockatrice and MTGO, and pickup games any hour. How Canadian Highlander is played online.
pageClass: play
permalink: /play/
---
<header class="page-head page-head--play">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Play</p>
    <h1 class="page-head__title">There's a game on <em>this weekend.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-head__lede">More than {{ play.discordMembers }} players. Two tournaments every week, three leagues every month, and someone looking for a match right now. No store, no travel, no entry fee.</p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--brass" href="{{ site.discord }}">Join the Discord</a>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="#weeklies">See the schedule <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tight" id="weeklies">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">§ 1 &nbsp;The weeklies</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Two tournaments. <em>Every weekend.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">Three Swiss rounds, fifty minutes each, then a final. No decklist to submit. Show up at start time, sign in on the Discord, and play whatever you brought.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="board">
      {%- for e in play.weeklies %}
      <article class="board__event" data-weekly data-day="{{ e.dayIndex }}" data-hour="{{ e.hour }}">
        <header class="board__top">
          <span class="board__day">{{ e.day }}</span>
          <span class="board__platform mono">{{ e.platform }}</span>
        </header>
        <p class="board__time"><span class="board__clock">10:00</span><span class="board__ampm">am Pacific</span></p>
        <p class="board__local mono" data-local>&nbsp;</p>
        <h3 class="board__name">{{ e.name }}</h3>
        <p class="board__blurb">{{ e.blurb }}</p>
        <dl class="board__facts">
          <div><dt>Rounds</dt><dd>3 + final</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Round clock</dt><dd>50 min</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Decklist</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <ol class="howto">
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">01</span><div><h3>Join and say hi</h3><p>Hop into the <a href="{{ site.discord }}">Discord</a> and find the tournament channels. Sign-ups and pairings are posted there, along with the full event rules.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">02</span><div><h3>Have your table ready</h3><p>Webcam events want a camera that can see your battlefield and a deck that's legal and sleeved. Cockatrice events want the free client installed and your list loaded.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">03</span><div><h3>Play your rounds</h3><p>Message your opponent, start the clock, report the result. Fifty minutes goes faster than you think.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="howto__n mono">04</span><div><h3>Make the final</h3><p>The best records after three rounds play it out. Strong finishes over the year can earn an invitation to the year-end invitational.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--felt" id="leagues">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">§ 2 &nbsp;Async leagues</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Can't do Saturday morning? <em>Play on your schedule.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__lede">Every month the Discord runs three asynchronous leagues. You get paired, you message your opponent, and the two of you play whenever suits you both before the round closes. Then the top eight play it out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="leagues">
      {%- for l in play.leagues %}
      <article class="league">
        <p class="league__platform mono">{{ l.platform }}</p>
        <h3 class="league__name">{{ l.name }}</h3>
        <p class="league__format">{{ l.format }}</p>
        <p class="league__lists"><span class="mono">Decklists</span> {{ l.lists }}</p>
        <p class="league__note">{{ l.note }}</p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="glossnote"><b>Locked</b> means you play the list you registered all month. <b>Open</b> means anyone can see it; <b>closed</b> means only the organizers can.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="pickup">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split__aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 3 &nbsp;Pickup games</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Want a game <em>right now?</em></h2>
      <p>Post in the looking-for-game channel with how you want to play: webcam, Cockatrice or MTGO. Someone is usually around, at most hours, in most time zones. Say if it's your first time. People will happily slow down, explain triggers, and tell you what that card you've never seen does.</p>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ site.discord }}">Find a match ↗</a>
    </div>
    <div class="lfg" aria-label="What to post when looking for a game">
      <p class="lfg__label mono">A good looking-for-game post</p>
      <p class="lfg__post"><span class="lfg__tag">LFG</span> Webcam · Boros Aggro · new to the format, happy to go slow</p>
      <ul class="lfg__parts">
        <li><b>How</b> webcam, Cockatrice or MTGO</li>
        <li><b>What</b> the deck you're bringing</li>
        <li><b>Who</b> first game, casual, or testing for the weekly</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule" id="tables">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 4 &nbsp;Pick your table</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Four ways to sit down.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tables">
      {%- for t in play.clients %}
      <a class="tablecard" href="{{ t.url }}">
        <span class="tablecard__kind mono">{{ t.kind }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__name">{{ t.name }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__desc">{{ t.desc }}</span>
        <span class="tablecard__cost mono">{{ t.cost }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--rule" id="proxies">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split__aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">§ 5 &nbsp;Proxies</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Nobody's checking <em>for a real Lotus.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The Discord's webcam tournaments are fully proxy-friendly. The only rules: a proxy has to show the card's full Oracle text, and it can't be something that could pass for a real card. A printout in a sleeve in front of a basic land is perfect.</p>
      <p>In paper, it depends on the store. Yellowjacket Comics in Victoria, where the format was born, allows ten proxies per deck. Plenty of other stores allow more. Ask before you sleeve up.</p>
      <p>Want a paper game near you? The community keeps a <a href="{{ site.official.home }}">worldwide list of regular events</a> linked from the official site, and the Discord has regional channels.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section cta-band">
  <div class="wrap cta-band__inner">
    <h2 class="h2">Saturday, 10 am Pacific. <em>Pull up a chair.</em></h2>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--brass" href="{{ site.discord }}">Join the Discord</a>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/decks/">Borrow a deck first <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
